================================================================================
pymatgen (the oracle of slice 1; no code copied)
================================================================================

Cells, expanded CIF sites, symmetry operations (spglib behind pymatgen),
d-spacings and the reflections within a sphere are checked against pymatgen
2026.9.24 / pymatgen-core 2026.9.23 by tools/slice-1/pins.py, whose output is
the committed fixture slice-1-pins.json. The Laue orbit and the absence rule are
computed from pymatgen's operations by the registration's definitions, in NumPy.

